   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> FAQ </h1>",
      "body": "<p>Frequently asked questions</p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c1720",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "Which tools can be measured with the »threadCheck ❘ cc«?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The »threadCheck ❘ cc« is specially designed for measuring threading tools and hobs with a pitch. The counter point enables us to achieve very precise concentricity.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1717",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "What are the advantages of the integrated tailstock?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>With the tailstock, long tools can be additionally guided or completely clamped between centers in order to achieve optimum stability during measurement. It also increases the concentricity of the tool.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1715",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "What measurements are possible with the swivel probe?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The optional swivel-mounted probe makes it possible to scan and evaluate the flank relief. In addition, parameters such as the rake angle, the pitch or the flute direction can be measured tactilely.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1713",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How are tools identified?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The »threadCheck ❘ cc« offers options for tool identification via RFID chips or DataMatrix codes to automatically retrieve and manage tool data.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1711",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "What automation solutions are available for the »threadCheck ❘ cc?«",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>In combination with the »roboSet 2« automation solution, tools can be loaded, measured and documented fully automatically.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1709",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Which interfaces are available?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The »threadCheck ❘ cc« has open data interfaces to transfer measurement data directly to CAD/CAM systems, grinding machines and tool management software.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1707",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How are the measurement results documented?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>All measurement results are documented in detail and can be passed on to customers as test reports to provide complete proof of tool quality.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1705",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How is the »threadCheck ❘ cc« integrated into production?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The »threadCheck ❘ cc« can be integrated directly into the production processes in order to transfer tool data from CAD/CAM systems and use target/actual comparisons for optimized grinding process control.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1703",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c1719",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
